# The flight screen's playback keys: FlightData.ProcessCmdKey's Space, which plays or pauses a
# loaded log (BUT_playlog_Click), and the keypad's - and +, which take LogPlayBackSpeed one down or
# up above 1 and halve or double it at 1 and under, then say it on lbl_playbackspeed
# (updateLogPlayPosition) (GCSViews/FlightData.cs:920-945, 5658-5685; crates/mp-gui/src/
# cmd_keys.rs, fly.rs Playback::step_speed). gpui names the keypad's keys apart on Linux, which
# xdotool's KP_Subtract and KP_Add press.
#
# The claim: a log given as the link plays at 1x; Space pauses it and plays it again; the keypad's
# - halves 1 to 0.5 and to 0.25, its + doubles back to 1, then 2, then one more, 3; the Telemetry
# Logs page says each speed. The main keyboard's - is not the keypad's, and does nothing.
#
# Plays the recorded copter flight, so it needs no vehicle. Run from the repository root:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-playback-keys.gui -- file:testdata/mavlink/autotest.tlog
#
# Not yet run: the budget is a guess, set by hand until a passing run records one.
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 8

expect fly.playback.file autotest.tlog
expect fly.playback.playing true
expect fly.playback.button Pause
expect fly.playback.speed x 1

# Space, with the window itself holding the keyboard: pause, then play.
key space
expect fly.playback.playing false
expect fly.playback.button Play
key space
expect fly.playback.playing true
expect fly.playback.button Pause

# The keypad's -: halved at 1 and under.
key KP_Subtract
expect fly.playback.speed x 0.5
key KP_Subtract
expect fly.playback.speed x 0.25

# The keypad's +: doubled up to 1 and 2, then one more.
key KP_Add
expect fly.playback.speed x 0.5
key KP_Add
expect fly.playback.speed x 1
key KP_Add
expect fly.playback.speed x 2
key KP_Add
expect fly.playback.speed x 3

# The main keyboard's minus is not Keys.Subtract.
key minus
expect fly.playback.speed x 3
key space
expect fly.playback.playing false
